  "id": "COMPOUND:17740 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "Murrayaquinone A is shown to have a target relationship with Raji through multiple pathways, with the most direct link being its interaction with Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is identified as a target of both Murrayaquinone A and another compound, CID 11603911, which in turn targets Raji. The evidence suggests that Murrayaquinone A may act on Microtubule-associated protein 1B to influence Raji cell behavior, potentially through mechanisms involving microtubule dynamics or protein interaction. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship with Raji indicates a possible role in cellular processes that are critical for Raji cell function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a central mediator in the biological effects of Murrayaquinone A on Raji cells.",
